>What weapon policy should I choose and what other advices could you give me?
> zefciu

As you noted, a Healer is not much of a melee character.  His best
offensive weapons tend to be the pets he surrounds himself with.

One advantage you have is that you're not going to run out of things to
eat, or food for you're pets, so you can stay take things slowly.

Don't enter a new level without being fully healed, and with the lack
of any other amulet, wear the "oESP constantly to give you warning.

If you carry around a diamond or another hard gem, you can engrave
semi-premanent "Elbereth" (carefully - it takes multiple turns.  Never
do it with a gem while being attacked)  In strategic places (the
upstairs, under piles of rocks, etc.) to create safe places for you to
recuperate, or barriers that most monsters won't pass.

If you have the patience, I would try to sac for a useful artifact.
(Mojo would be perfect for you.  That's what I got when I ascended my
healer, but any one of the "useful" artifact would be better than a
unihorn, and allow you to wear a small shield).   Being able to deal
out a decent amount of damage per turn is important.

In general, you're doing fine.  Finish the mines (carefully!!), and go
for the quest.  When you get there (think positive!) I would suggest
reading some spoilers about the nemesis, and how to avoid dying to him.

Good Luck.
